uncilmembers Groveman, Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Bartlett, Colantuono, Coroalles, Lysik, Peirce.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Gary Lysik.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, stated that the Council did not take any action in closed session which required reporting. \r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\r Mayor pro Tem Bozajian announced that the �State of the City� address will be taking place on January 24, 2007. He also spoke regarding the City of Calabasas General Municipal Election on March 6 and announced absentee ballot period information. Mayor Washburn announced the Annual Calabasas Chamber of Commerce Luncheon will be occurring on January 25, 2007.\r\r\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r No one indicated a desire to speak.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the December 6, 2006 City Council meeting. \r\r Recommendation to approve a professional services agreement with Venco Western, Inc. for Street Sweeping Services in the amount not to exceed $130,398.\r\r Annual allocations of Proposition C Funds to capital reserve account for a transit facility.\r\r Recommendation to approve a professional services agreement with Rincon Consultants in an amount of $1,224,335 for preparation of the General Plan update, General Plan Environmental Impact Report, and Development Code update.\r\r Recommendation to accept completion of Brandon�s Village at Gates Canyon Park, by Shane�s Inspiration; and direct the City Clerk to file the notice of completion.\r \r Upgrade to existing landscaping on upper Parkway Calabasas median.\r\r Recommendation from staff and the Civic Center Task Force to award additive and deductive bid alternates to Bernards Brothers Inc. in the amount of $199,000.00, increasing the contract duration to 520 days.\r\r Approval of a salary adjustment for the position of Chief Financial Officer.\r\rMayor pro Tem Bozajian \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 and 8. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rSPECIAL ITEM\r\r Presentation by Sadina Reynaldo, PhD from the Los Angeles County Department of Health regarding Pandemic Flu.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\r Presentation by United States Postal Service representatives from the Woodland Hills Post Office regarding service issue and complaint procedures.\r\rStacia Crane, Customer Service Representative, United States Postal Service, provided information on service issues.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r\r Review and approval of projects for the 33rd Program Year (2007-2008) � Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) Funding; and adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1061, approving the CDBG 33rd Program Year (2007-2008).\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Mayor Washburn opened the public hearing.\r\r Mayor Washburn closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to approve projects for the 33rd Program Year (2007-2008) � Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) Funding; and adopt Resolution No. 2007-1061, approving the CDBG 33rd Program Year (2007-2008). MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Recommendation to approve a City employee home buying incentive program.\r\rThe City Council directed the City Manager to develop a home buying incentive program and return to the City Council for approval. \r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Check Register for the period of November 29, 2006 to January 4, 2007.\r\rNo action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r There were no task force reports.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r The City Manager indicated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r The City Council requested the following items on future agendas:\r\rAn item regarding investigating the hiring/contracting of a mediator; and \rA report regarding cell phone 